/** Translation maps for siman 043 — imported by _patch-siman-043.mjs */
export const TRANSLATIONS = {
  mechaber: {
    '1#main': `The laws of treifot regarding the spleen. In it are 6 seifim. If the spleen was removed — kosher.`,
    '2#main': `The spleen: one end is thick and the other thin, like the creation of the tongue. If it was punctured in the thick end — if the hole is a perforation through and through — treifah. If punctured with a hole that is not a perforation through and through — if there remains beneath it like the thickness of a gold dinar — permitted; less than this is considered as if perforated and treifah. But if the thin end was punctured — kosher. {Rama: And even if it was cut off in the thin place — kosher (Tur). If the spleen was torn, or putrefied, or afflicted with a change of flesh — its law is like punctured (Shaarei Dura and Hagahot Asheri). And so everywhere the flesh is bad and rotted — its law is like punctured. And if there is water in the spleen — even if murky and putrid — if the flesh around it is whole — kosher (Beit Yosef in the name of Mordechai and Hagahot Asheri, and see above siman 50).}`,
    '3#main': `There is one who wrote that everything attached to the kereis is called "thick" and nothing more.`,
    '4#main': `The thickness of a gold dinar — we do not know its measure; nevertheless it appears that it is less than half its thickness.`,
    '5#main': `If two spleens were found — kosher, even if attached to each other on the thick side. {Rama: And some are stringent if something like a spleen is found on the thick side (Hagahot ShDa siman 89 and Mateh Moshe in the name of Maharil and Mahari Molinus). And it is good to be stringent if not in a place of great loss.}`,
    '6#main': `The spleen of fowl is round like a grape and is not similar to that of an animal; therefore a hole does not disqualify it.`,
  },
  'siftei-kohen': {
    '2#א': `"And if it was punctured with a hole that is not a perforation through and through," etc. This is Rashi's language: "And if there remained in the thickness of its wall and the needle did not come out — and there is a covering opposite it like the thickness of a dinar — kosher," end of his words. And so it is in Hagahot ShDa siman 89. And it is simple that we are not now dealing with the law of a needle found in the body cavity, but rather he cited a needle as an example — you find it when you insert it before us and it strikes the spleen, for it is known that none of the inner organs were punctured, as below siman 51. And Bach forced himself on this and explained a strange, far-fetched explanation — see there.`,
    '2#ב': `"And even if it was cut off," etc. Meaning: in the thin place it is more reasonable to declare treifah if cut than if punctured — he teaches us that nevertheless it is kosher. But in the thick place there is a dispute among the poskim whether if cut it is treifah; and the Mechaber's view and the Rav's view appear that it is treifah, as written in Beit Yosef and Darkei Moshe, and so Maharshal Piskei Avodah Zarah siman 85 and the acharonim.`,
    '2#ג': `"If it was torn," etc. All of this refers to its thick head — and this is simple.`,
    '2#ד': `"With a change of flesh." Because we consider it as if it had dissolved, for we are not expert in scraping that doctors scrape, as below siman 50. But a change of appearance alone is kosher — for specifically when it fell to light is it treifah, when the spleen reddened like a pomegranate in its hilum, below siman 52. And so is the view of Maharshal and Bach.`,
    '2#ה': `"If the flesh around it is whole," etc. This implies when there remained in it like the thickness of a gold dinar — for the above refers to this. And so wrote Turei Chayim kelal 89 din 1 explicitly. And so Peri Megadim, not like Bach who wrote that the Rav in the hagahah retracted from what he wrote in Turei Chayim and permitted even if there did not remain like the thickness of a gold dinar. And even what he challenged afterward — why do we permit more in murky and putrid than in putrefied — enters with difficulty into his approach; but in truth there is no difficulty, for also in murky and putrid we require that there remain like the thickness of a gold dinar.`,
    '3#_': `That everything attached, etc. See in Sefer Lechem Chamudos daf 168b an incident that occurred in the community of Prague regarding this.`,
    '4#_': `Less than half its thickness. Of that spleen in the place where it is thick — and see above siman 46 seif 3.`,
    '5#א': `"And even if attached to each other on the thick side." For he holds that what we say "all excess is considered as removed" means as if both were removed from their place — and the spleen removed is kosher.`,
    '5#ב': `"And some are stringent," etc. In Darkei Moshe and Turei Chayim kelal 89 din 3 he wrote that this is because he holds like the Ramban (and in the hagahah at the end of Orach Chaim not so — see in Hagahot Darkei Moshe) that Rashba and other poskim brought: "all excess is considered as removed" means as if the excess alone was removed from its attached place — and it is as if the spleen was punctured in its hilum. And Bach ruled that one must declare treifah even in great loss, like Rashba. And in my humble opinion they are certainly worthy — Rashi, Rosh, Rambam, Tur, and Rabbenu Yerucham and Beit Yosef — to rely on them in great loss.`,
    '6#_': `Therefore a hole does not disqualify it. And Ra'ah in Beit Habechirah daf 50 forbids; and so appears the view of Ran; and so Maharshal Piskei Avodah Zarah siman 85 is stringent; and so Bach wrote one should be stringent for himself — and see above end of siman 44.`,
  },
  'turei-zahav': {
    '2#א': `In the thick head. It appears that even though on the side of the thick there is also somewhat thin in width, nevertheless it is forbidden there — for otherwise he would not have said "thick head" but "part of the thick"; rather everything on that side is forbidden.`,
    '2#ב': `A perforation through and through — treifah. It appears simple that even if the skin on the spleen was not punctured there — treifah — for that skin is not included in "spleen" plain, but has another name, namely the membrane on the spleen mentioned in siman 64 seif 10. And as they said: if the heart was punctured — treifah — it is obvious they did not mean that the membrane on it must also be punctured; so too here with the spleen — certainly it does not help to permit that the membrane on it remained intact. And further proof from the words of Orach Chaim HaAruch that I brought in siman 46 seif 1 — see there. I was asked: in a certain district of calves there are perforations through and through in the spleen at the thick head, and around the hole from inside the spleen skin surrounds it and it is recognizable that it was created so; and each time the hole is found in one place, and some people say that thus is the way of most calves there. I answered to permit — for needless to say according to those poskim who hold that deficiency from the body of the lung is kosher, as in siman 36 seif 8 — namely when there is deficiency and crack in the lung and the skin and flesh remain — so too here it is kosher; for there it is forbidden with a hole even if not through and through, yet we say since the skin beneath remains there is no hole on it — so too here with through and through: thus I understand the lung without through and through like the spleen with through and through. And just as in the lung it is not called a hole as long as the membrane remains — so too in the spleen with through and through. And further: there too we find through and through yet kosher, e.g. when there is deficiency at the bottom of the lung and the skin is whole around it — we say there it is kosher, only that in some places they practice to declare treifah if it is like a bent palm; and in many places they permit in every case, as written there in the name of Maharshal. And even for Rambam who forbids the lung, and they wrote in Shulchan Aruch there in the name of "some forbid" — the prohibition is not on account of a hole but on account of deficiency, as they mentioned there in the language of deficiency. And so is proven further from what Rambam wrote that Shulchan Aruch copied siman 50 seif 2: "Every organ we said — if punctured in any amount treifah; so too if all of it was removed treifah, whether removed through illness or created deficient," etc. — behold he did not mention this "whether created deficient" except regarding removal, and they did not mention it regarding puncture that he opened with it; rather necessarily there is no relevance of "hole" if created so, but there is deficiency upon it — therefore Rambam forbade the lung, for a lung that is deficient is treifah; and this too is included in "removed." Not so the spleen — if it is deficient it is kosher, as explained here: what difference to me if all of it is deficient or part of it. If so, this round hole created so is in the category of deficiency and kosher in the spleen, and there is no prohibition except if punctured afterward — for we say the blow of the hole will cause damage to the rest of the body, as Rashi in the Gemara. Not so here where there is no blow but deficiency alone — kosher, in my humble opinion.`,
    '2#ג': `Like the thickness of a dinar. It appears that thickness must be specifically from the flesh of the spleen itself, and sealing of the lung or flesh does not help, as in siman 45 in the name of Orach Chaim.`,
    '2#ד': `But if the thin end was punctured — kosher. It appears clear that those holes in the spleen that are kosher refer when there is no needle placed before us there — for if there is a needle it is certainly no better than liver or tarfesha of liver, for there is concern perhaps it entered from outside after the esophagus was punctured, as we are concerned with liver in siman 41 seif 6 — specifically regarding lung it was permitted according to Talmudic law since it is close to the windpipe and from there the needle went to it; and so in the stomach, as stated siman 48, that there we say the way of the esophagus is to reach it, even in the outer pouch of food and drink that they forced, as stated explicitly in the Gemara; and so in the crop, as above siman 41 seif 6 — liver is not comparable to all these. And the spleen is certainly comparable to liver in this, for all the stringencies they said regarding a needle in liver apply to the spleen, which is farther from the windpipe than even the liver. And I saw Maharshal brought Rashi's words Piskei Avodah Zarah (daf 55): "And if there remained in the thickness of its wall like the thickness of a dinar and the needle did not come out — and there is a covering opposite it like the thickness of a dinar — kosher." And from this he distinguished: if the needle is found in the thickness of the inner spleen attached to the kereis — we attribute that the way of the esophagus enters the kereis and food and drink forced it and it entered the spleen; therefore if there remained like the thickness of the dinar in the thickness of the spleen toward the outside — kosher, for it is no worse than if punctured — and liver seals its hole and is kosher; so too the spleen attached to the kereis — the spleen seals the hole. But if a needle is found in its loose end toward the outside — even if there remained like the thickness of a dinar in the place attached to the kereis — treifah, like a needle found in the body cavity of the animal, end of his words. And in my humble opinion it is clear that the spleen does not seal a hole in the kereis, as I proved in siman 48 seif 2. And Rashi who cited here a needle found in the spleen refers when there is no concern that other inner organs were punctured, as Mordechai wrote siman 50 and 51 — namely that we saw it came from the outside toward the spleen; but in an unspecified case where a needle is found in the spleen in every manner — treifah, for the Sages did not distinguish to permit a needle only in lung, liver, crop, melting organ, and stomach — and they did not mention anything of the spleen if there were a distinction; certainly they would not have been silent about it — rather certainly in every manner treifah. It appears to me simple in reason that the spleen does not help to seal a hole in the kereis at all.`,
    '2#ה': `Afflicted with a change of flesh. Maharshal wrote that a change of appearance does not disqualify at all in the spleen, for this is not found at all in the Talmud. And it appears that Rama here too did not forbid except when the flesh is afflicted on account of the change; but on account of change alone there is no treifah — and so wrote Maharshal.`,
    '2#ו': `And if there is water in the spleen, etc. The source of this law is from Mordechai Piskei Avodah Zarah, and this is his language: Rabbi Yitzchak of Vienna wrote: I saw before our teacher Rabbeinu Ephraim that they brought before him a cow's spleen very swollen in its middle until its hilum; he commanded and they cut before him the swelling; when they cut, clear water jumped from the spleen from the place of the swelling and water the amount of a large vessel came out; its appearance inside was like wax; he commanded and they scraped inside with a knife and scraped much and examined inside and it was whole on every side that it was not punctured; and Rabbeinu Ephraim told us that Rabbenu Tam said to Raavan mouth to mouth in every place the Sages said it is treifah through a hole — even if it was not punctured and the flesh around it is bad it is treifah; and here since they scraped it inside and it was found whole on every side — it appears to permit. And he said that if the water were putrid he would also permit, end of his words. And one may wonder why Rabbi Yitzchak needed to write this incident — for even if cut entirely on the thin side it is kosher; why would there be treifah here when the swelling was only until the hilum. And it appears he wrote it to inform us two things: one, that at that time Rabbeinu Ephraim told him what he heard from Rabbenu Tam that if the flesh is bad it is like punctured — from this we learn that if so on the thick side and dinar-thickness did not remain whole it is treifah. Two, that we do not say since it rotted so much until it became water — and all the more if putrid — perhaps in the end it will be afflicted in all of it including the hilum; he teaches that since it only went until the hilum and from there onward there is no affliction at all — kosher. From this we learn that if there is affliction in the spleen on the thick side, i.e. the hilum, it is certainly treifah if above or below dinar-thickness did not remain — this affliction is like punctured or cut, as Rabbenu Tam told Raavan; and even if the water were clear, nevertheless it is affliction and is considered at least deficiency in that place. And what Rabbeinu Ephraim permitted here if the flesh is whole means it remained whole in the hilum in its measure — and so is written in Turei Chayim explicitly; and so is Rama's intent here in what he wrote "if the flesh is whole," meaning in its law in the hilum; and he teaches that whenever there is water in the spleen they do not forbid — even if putrid we do not say perhaps in the end all will rot; nevertheless we require that the whole flesh be in its measure, namely the hilum shall be like a dinar. And behold Maharshal wrote that from Rama's words here it implies that even if dinar-thickness did not remain in the hilum, nevertheless kosher — and he retracts from what he wrote in Turei Chayim; and I do not know who inserted this to separate between the attached parts — but in truth Rama's words here and in Turei Chayim are one, and so is the essence: everywhere flesh is missing in the thick place — even through clear water there is no permit unless dinar-thickness remained from it, as above.`,
    '4#_': `That it is less than half its thickness. The reason: in the Gemara they said regarding this "if there remained like the thickness of a dinar" — and every remainder is less than half of it.`,
    '5#_': `On the thick side, etc. For he holds that what they said "all excess is considered as removed" means from the place where it is attached there — as if that place was removed; and this is the Ramban's view that I mentioned siman 55 seif 4. And Maharshal ruled so in Piskei Avodah Zarah siman 18 — and so Maharshal — and even in great loss one may rule so.`,
    '6#_': `Therefore a hole does not disqualify it. And Maharshal wrote Piskei Avodah Zarah siman 85 that it is a great leniency to uproot the principle they said: everything that makes treifah in an animal — the corresponding in fowl; and the opposite is reasonable — everything is called hilum in fowl. And in Maharil he did not permit affliction in the entire kidney of fowl even though its form is not at all like that of an animal, but because they are closed in bone and the intestines do not reach there — if so, spleen of fowl which is in the place of intestines is treifah like in an animal; nevertheless since Rashba already ruled leniency, an elder has taught leniency — I do not forbid those who permit and rely on his ruling; but Heaven forbid for us to permit ab initio, end of his words. And Maharshal corrected Rambam's words: since they said in the Gemara "treifot that the Sages enumerated in an animal — corresponding in fowl," namely what they enumerated in the mishnah — and spleen and kidney were not enumerated in the mishnah. And it is difficult — for we find this language again in the Gemara (daf 54): in the house of Rav Pappa they struck the kidney and killed it; it came before Rabbi Abba; he said to them: is there adding to the treifot? You have only what the Sages enumerated — and that certainly does not refer to the mishnah alone but to all that the Amoraim enumerated. If so, from where to distinguish and explain there a different matter? Also Ra'ah in Beit Habechirah wrote to forbid in fowl — therefore every person of spirit should be stringent for himself in this. It appears to me that what they forbade through putrefaction or affliction on the thick side is specifically when it begins from outside and goes inward; but if the spleen outside is whole and afflicted inside — there is no prohibition, for it is not stricter than lung where we say internal deficiency is not called deficiency — and know from that they said in the Gemara: kosher in lung, invalid in kidney — namely putrefied; and they did not say so in spleen where invalid in it what is kosher in lung, namely regarding internal deficiency. And so appears Maharshal's view in what he cited in his name in siman 44 seif 2; nevertheless I fear to be lenient since it is not explicit in the poskim.`,
  },
  'baer-heitev': {
    '2#א': `Through and through. Taz wrote it appears simple that even if the skin of the spleen was not punctured there — treifah — for the skin is not included in "spleen" plain but has another name, namely the membrane on the spleen. And he wrote further that even though on the thick side there is also somewhat thin in width, nevertheless it is forbidden there — for otherwise he would have said only "part of the thick" but all on that side is forbidden; and so wrote Shlah daf 75. And on the thin side too there is no distinction even if somewhat thick — nevertheless it is called the thin side. And Taz wrote further: I was asked regarding calves in a certain district that have a perforation through and through in the spleen at the thick head and around the hole from inside the spleen skin surrounds and it is recognizable it was created so; each time the hole is found in one place; some say thus is the way of most calves — I answered to permit — see there his reason. And Nekudat HaKesef disagrees and wrote such an incident came to him and he declared treifah (and in Turei Chayim Chiddushei Basra question 43 and Be'er HaGolah question 120 and Pri Chadash and Pri Megadim also disagree on Taz).`,
    '2#ב': `Like thickness. Taz wrote that thickness must be specifically from the flesh of the spleen itself and sealing of milk or flesh does not help. (Also the membrane on it does not combine, for it is not included in "spleen" plain.)`,
    '2#ג': `Kosher. Taz and Shach wrote it appears clear that those holes in the spleen that are kosher refer when there is no needle placed before us; if there is a needle it is certainly no better than liver and treifah. And what Rashi wrote "and if there remained and the needle did not come out" — it must refer to the law of a needle: namely we inserted it before us and it struck the spleen, for it is known none of the inner organs were punctured. (Spleen that was salted without nikkur is permitted — presumably there is 60 against the prohibition in it, siman 85. Bach wrote even if there is 60 one needs peeling around the cavity of the spleen. Taz siman 87 wrote that by law it is forbidden until the spleen and forbidden fat in it are certainly 60 against the nikkur.)`,
    '2#ד': `And rotted. Taz wrote what they forbade through putrefaction or affliction on the thick side is specifically when it begins from outside and goes inward; but if the spleen outside is whole and afflicted inside — no prohibition (internal deficiency is not called deficiency), for it is not stricter than lung; and so appears Maharshal's view, but nevertheless I fear to be lenient since it is not explicit in poskim, end of his words. (If cut in the thick place — treifah — acharonim. Change of appearance does not disqualify the spleen except specifically when it fell to light — treifah when the spleen reddened like a pomegranate — and see below siman 52 Shach.)`,
    '2#ה': `Whole. Shach wrote one must have remain like the thickness of a gold dinar — not like Bach who permits even less than the thickness of a gold dinar.`,
    '4#_': `Its thickness. Meaning: of that spleen in the thick place.`,
    '5#_': `Great loss. The reason of the lenient: for according to what we hold "all excess is considered as removed" — as if both were removed and the spleen removed is kosher; and this is the view of Rashi, Rambam, and Rosh. Bach and Maharshal ruled one must be stringent and declare treifah even in great loss. Shach ruled like Rama's view who holds "all excess is considered as removed" means from the place where it is attached — as if that place was removed — and it is as if the spleen was punctured in its hilum; and this is the Ramban's view. Animal that had two spleens and one of them was punctured in the hilum — Taz Taz siman 98 ruled: if recognizable which is primary and it was not punctured — kosher; if not recognizable — treifah from doubt; and Pri Chadash wrote in every manner one must declare treifah.`,
    '6#_': `The hole. Maharshal forbids spleen of fowl in every place it was punctured, for all is called hilum. Taz wrote a person of spirit should be stringent for himself (and Pri Chadash wrote in every manner one must declare treifah — and all this in fowl; but in animal and wild animal, whether large or small, their law is equal — from what is stated daf 146).`,
  },
  'beer-hagolah': {
    '1#_': `Mishnah Chullin daf 54.`,
    '2#_': `Conclusion of the Gemara according to Rav Avira there daf 55.`,
    '3#_': `Rambam's language in chapter 6 of Hilchot Shechitah; (°) and in Torat Chatat he ruled specifically like the thickness of a gold dinar.`,
    '4#_': `Hagahot Asheri; and so wrote Rabbenu Yerucham (and Mordechai and Hagahot ShDa siman 89 and Orach Chaim kelal 52 din 11).`,
    '5#_': `Tur in the name of Rashba in Teshuvot HaKetzarot; and he concludes there regarding "there remained" he spoke.`,
    '6#_': `Rambam in chapter 6 of Hilchot Shechitah.`,
  },
  'beur-hagra': {
    '2#א': `"And even if it was cut off," etc. Mishnah at end of chapter 4 of the spleen, etc.; and it is not necessary for the latter version there 55a except even for the first version — namely according to the view that we do not distinguish between hilum and loose end; but according to us the mishnah is in the loose end, as Ran wrote; and it is implied from the hagahah words that if cut in the hilum it is invalid as above — even for the latter version, for according to us this is unnecessary; and all the more the first version — see Ran. (Likut) "And even if cut off," etc. — in Beit Ephraim he wrote even if cut in the thick place kosher, like the latter version; but in Teshuvot HaRashba he disagreed, for in his responsa he followed the stringent (end of his words).`,
    '2#ב': `"Afflicted," etc. See above siman 50.`,
    '2#ג': `"And if water," etc. Peri Megadim and Shach wrote specifically if dinar-thickness remained; but Pri Chadash wrote since whole on every side it is unnecessary; and so regarding punctured.`,
    '5#_': `"And some are stringent." This is the Ramban and Be'er HaGolah; but the first reason holds as if both were removed.`,
    '6#_': `(Likut) Spleen of fowl, etc. From what is stated (56a) "treifot that the Sages enumerated in an animal — corresponding in fowl" — and spleen and kidneys were not enumerated in the animal for prohibition; and see Teshuvot HaRashba 35b (end of his words).`,
  },
  'kereti': {
    '2#א': `Perforation through and through in calves at the thick head — perforation through and through and skin surrounds it and it is in one place and recognizable it was created so: Taz and Taz permit; many disagree, headed by Shach in Nekudat HaKesef and Pri Chadash; and I inclined Peleti that I elaborated on this. If not always in one place — certainly treifah; but if always in one place I never permitted in this — only leave to rule one whose heart does not strike him; and where there is no man one may rely in great loss on Taz and his support.`,
    '2#ב': `Like thickness of gold dinar from the body of the spleen and not from pure fat that seals — and the like — Taz.`,
    '2#ג': `Treifah — see Peleti that I wrote in the name of acharonim: if punctured from kereis to spleen the spleen does not seal the kereis, for impure fat and membranes forbid and separate and they do not seal — see Peleti in explanation of Rashi's words that he wrote punctured via needle; although he explained the matter "insert before us" — nevertheless what did Rashi want with this.`,
    '2#ד': `"And even if cut off" — see Peleti that I elaborated in pilpul on "even"; for Baal HaItur's view is to permit if cut even in the hilum — see there and in explanation of Beit Ephraim's words.`,
    '2#ה': `With change of flesh — but change of appearance does not disqualify unless it fell to light — and this is simple.`,
    '2#ו': `Even murky and putrid — even though he cited; but one law: clear water with murky — see Peleti what he wrote.`,
    '2#ז': `And the flesh around it whole — see Peleti that I wrote he intended Taz's words: if the spleen is whole on every side outside and only afflicted inside — even if no gold dinar, because since whole the name "hole" does not apply to it and we learned "punctured" in the mishnah; and if the flesh is bad only the membrane on it is whole — that helps only if the flesh of the spleen too is whole on every side — see Peleti.`,
    '3#_': `And nothing more — in Lechem Mishneh he was uncertain: if so, what is attached to the kereis specifically and the rest is in the category of loose end or the main half of it; and if you divide the spleen in two there will be a thick place more than what is attached to the kereis. See Peleti what he wrote to decide: if clear to us there is no remainder of gold dinar — treifah; but if we are uncertain here too — one must be stringent — see his name.`,
    '4#א': `Thickness of gold dinar — see Peleti that I found its measure is no more than a third of a finger, which is two finger-widths and a half — see his name.`,
    '4#ב': `Less than half thickness — see Peleti, not like Perishah in Kuntres Aleph that his view is the thickness of spleen from the calf suffices even in a large ox — Heaven forbid to be lenient with such a leniency; and see Peleti on this; and this requires further study.`,
    '5#א': `Two spleens — see Taz: if two spleens found and known which spleen is correct and which is excess and punctured in hilum — kosher; and he learned this from kidneys; and there too Maharshal obtained — see Peleti that I elaborated.`,
    '5#ב': `On the thick side, etc. — this is the Ramban's view who holds excess is considered as removed like a hole in that place — and punctured in hilum is treifah.`,
    '6#_': `Fowl — see Peleti that I clarified one may rely on this without hesitation, as Rashba wrote: an elder has already taught leniency.`,
  },
  peleti: {
    '2#א': `If punctured in the thick head, etc. — Taz wrote regarding calves that at the thick head there is perforation through and through and skin surrounds it; in every calf found thus in one place, and people say thus is the way of most calves there — Taz ruled to permit, for this is not a hole but deficiency and kosher; and in responsa Taz he explained his words: in hollow things a hole applies even if created so, but in a flat thing like a leaf a hole does not apply if created so — what difference to me if created deficient at the end of the spleen or in its middle. Taz agreed to permit. Shach in Nekudat HaKesef and Pri Chadash ruled to forbid. One argument: who says it was only at creation and afterward through weakness became so healthy until it looks created — this can be answered since we see all in one directed place, a sign it was made so in nature; if by illness and accident it would not always be in one directed place. In Rashba's responsa siman 483 intestinal holes were not directed in all animals in one place — therefore no proof it was a hole in the small intestine that Rashba doubted whether made afterward by illness or before; there it was not directed in one place, but in the body of the heter there is no hole if created so — I am uncertain from two proofs. One: Rashba wrote if two spleens and one attached to its fellow in hilum — according to "considered removed" with the place of its attachment — treifah, as if removed from hilum and as if hole and treifah; though from creation considered removed, nevertheless treifah — this can be rejected: "considered removed" is tradition from the Sages, and tradition is that for Rabbi extra spleens cause weakness as if in that attached place something was missing and removed somewhat by hand — treifah from weakness in two spleens attached where they make treifah for the animal as if called so now and treifah; and they were precise from that he said "considered removed" and not "considered deficient." Second proof: Tosafot and Rosh and authors were precise that mishnah did not enumerate removed heart, stomach, etc. — all the more from punctured; and mishnah "punctured the omasum" — Rabbi says even if removed — implies more to permit in punctured than removed; they challenged from "if so" and entered with difficulty. Seemingly simple: certainly if punctured treifah, all the more removed — not necessary, for Rashi wrote punctured is stricter than removed because through hole it continues and adds pain and much illness in the body — this applies to hole by hand and illness, but created with hole Rashi's words do not apply, there is no pain and illness — plainly one may say if punctured treifah, all the more removed; so in heart and stomach and the like which are hollow organs where hole applies even at beginning of creation, as Taz wrote, the poskim's "all the more" applies even not from pain — but in spleen where hole at creation does not apply, as Taz, only in category removed; if you find hole in spleen only through illness and thorn — here there is no "all the more" for removed as Rashi. However one may say conversely: from Tosafot's precision from Rashi who wrote therefore punctured treifah and removed spleen kosher because it adds illness and pain — created with hole from "if so" wherever "punctured" is said even if created so, for there is no pain — necessarily Rashi holds hole at creation does not apply to spleen, as Taz; and this requires further study. Truth: I always inclined to be stringent in doubt of law; only this I gave my heart: as Taz and Taz wrote, all was in calves and many such questions came in calves; in oxen and cows such a question was never mentioned — only once. It is astounding: if common in calves, it should be common in oxen and cows, for a calf becomes an ox when it grows. From this I judged: when the animal grows the hole heals and deficiency fills and flesh returns as before — therefore not felt in a large animal; hence a sign it is not absolute treifah — how would it heal if treifah, and how always membrane from a blow; rather nature did not complete creation and deficiency is found, and in many days deficiency fills — very conceivable to naturalists; therefore my view tends to permit; nevertheless I never permitted all my days — only leave others to permit whose heart does not strike them; where there is no man one may not permit except in great loss and great investigation needed.`,
    '2#ב': `Perforation through and through. Rashi explained: if there remained like thickness of gold dinar and needle did not come out. Bach wants to save from difficulty that it would be needle in body cavity — explained hole via kereis and spleen attached seals it. True Rashi did not hold as below siman 46 seif 1 in hagahah that another organ does not seal, as appears from Rashi daf 49b s.v. tarfesha; nevertheless impure fat separates between spleen and kereis and it is like a hat and does not seal, for there is space on the hole and it is not tight inside the hole — what does it help that spleen is attached and seals? Therefore all agreed we deal with needle in body cavity inserted before us — no further concern for other inner organs; true for law, but I am not released: why did Rashi need needle inserted before us and not simply punctured through illness and putrefaction as daily practice? I said much and did not succeed that it be close to Rashi's intent; what appears most: difficult for Rashi the Gemara language "if there remained like gold dinar kosher" — implies to permit it came with dinar remainder kosher; in truth reversed — unspecified hole is perforation through and through everywhere in all treifot; if not Gemara words, even any remainder like egg membrane would be kosher — Gemara was stringent to require dinar thickness; what does it teach kosher — as if coming to teach us a permitted prohibition? It should say: and if dinar-thickness did not remain treifah — do not say regarding perforation through and through. Therefore Rashi holds we deal with needle; Rashi holds in melting organ since it has only one membrane we fear perhaps it healed — not regarding perforation through and through; if so also in spleen hole with needle one need not perforation through and through at all — we fear perhaps it healed; therefore Gemara in spleen only says if dinar-thickness remained kosher — and teaches much to permit: we do not forbid hole that is not perforation through and through; examine well; Rashi's words are clear.`,
    '2#ג': `And even if cut off, etc. — many wondered what "even"; for one version punctured treifah and cut kosher — so Baal HaItur. It appears Baal HaEphraim ruled cut even in hilum kosher as one version in Gemara that answers on mishnah chapter Behemah Hamaksheh: cutting from fetus permitted from spleen and kidneys forbidden — animal permitted; answers even animal forbidden; if so punctured alone cut alone — this version Baal HaEphraim seized; Rashba wondered why he ruled leniently like second version. So Rashba to Rashi beginning chapter Behemah Hamaksheh (and so R' Akiva of Bertinoro): therefore cited spleen and kidneys immediately because not treifah in them; wrote Rashi holds like Baal HaEphraim halacha like latter version; but Ran wrote since we hold to distinguish hilum and loose end we need not all this and no distinction between punctured and cut; so Pri Chadash; and he challenged Chavot Yair who also challenged Rashba; truly Rashba and Ran were hidden from Chavot Yair who did not mention them; afterward brought in Darkei Moshe. It appears Baal HaEphraim and Rashba were not hidden from Ran's reasons — simple one may say cut in loose end; difficult for Rashi why cited spleen — if not treifah in them cite liver which also not treifah if cut and left olive for each as he has; mishnah need not inform cutting entire organ unlike liver needing remainder for each and impossible to cut entire liver; in spleen deals with cutting entire spleen without remainder — kosher for all — removed spleen; if so no place for Gemara difficulty on removed entire spleen kosher without distinction; language "cut from spleen" implies not entire spleen; so Pri Chadash seif 4; mishnah did not cite entire spleen — teaches slaughter does not permit, needs whole animal not deficient as Rashi; possible deficiency of entire organ but animal has all organs — all the more partial cut majority as whole called whole — teaches not; this is simple; mishnah did not want to settle laws — liver must not be cut in place of bile and life, etc.; stam "cut" anywhere; difficult also spleen needs condition not cut in hilum — must hold mishnah does not distinguish; properly cut kosher even in hilum; therefore Rashba only challenged from first answer in Gemara; in first version harder: answers what mishnah teaches forbidden in eating applies to animal — only because animal treifah why not cite liver or kidneys alone — for Rish Lakish teaches much: forbidden in eating — slaughter does not permit limb from living; certainly if animal treifah obviously forbidden — does slaughter help to permit treifah? Only teaches slaughter does not help because of limb from living; this depends on dispute — Rava is author of removed spleen; holds below end 23 if tore organ and made treifah — Rish Lakish liable for limb from living, R' Yochanan two liabilities treifah and limb from living; one may say mishnah incidentally teaches forbidden only for limb from living like kidneys where only limb-from-living prohibition; like Rish Lakish who holds only limb from living applies. More likely teaches liable for limb from living; R' Yochanan Chullin 102b not liable except for meat in field treifah; if ate with treifah meat only one set of lashes as Rambam Hilchot Ma'achalot Assurot chapter 10; difficult what mishnah teaches forbidden — obviously forbidden, all animal forbidden; if for limb from living that is treifah meat — one prohibition; see chapter 8 Hilchot Ma'achalot Assurot; Rambam wanted to resolve this and holds organ without bone like spleen lashes for limb from living — behold two prohibitions; for Raavad who holds also only meat in field, etc. — difficulty stands; must say Gemara version comes for Rish Lakish who holds all lashes for limb from living — Baal HaEphraim's view; since halacha like R' Yochanan — first version gone; since we hold like R' Yochanan and second version — Baal HaEphraim justified. Further on Rashi who wrote spleen not treifah — difficult for our view we say treifah; nevertheless cited spleen; why not cite liver — they challenged on rule wherever punctured treifah also removed from spleen; answer spleen different — not treifah in hole only in hilum; difficult for our view that challenges from Behemah Hamaksheh implies all hold hole disqualifies — how did poskim understand difficulty. Must understand their version: even in hilum hole difficult; if entire spleen with hilum removed kosher; certainly in hilum treifah from affliction reaching kereis attached — through affliction rot and affliction reach kereis and treifah; therefore when not attached kosher; if so plainly rule if punctured disqualifies all the more removed — if from itself implies life in it — how permit in removed what life depends on; not so spleen where hole from kereis — kosher in removed when not attached to kereis, kereis not harmed; one may say even our view knew all treifot of hole from kereis — even below attachment place since one side lost and half attached to kereis — if affliction below weakness spreads until kereis place and there treifah and destroys kereis — no difficulty between punctured and removed; and understand Rashi and mishnah why not cite liver — mishnah teaches slaughter does not permit its organs, needs whole animal; one may err organs life depends on them — they belong to animal without them not animal and treifah; organ life not dependent — without it also alive — called whole; see Eruchin "one who vows value of liver since life depends on it — value of whole" unlike other organs — teaches nevertheless slaughter does not permit; Rashi's intent cited spleen and kidneys not treifah in them — even if spleen punctured in hilum treifah from kereis but in itself no life — not relevant to animal therefore did not cite liver removed entirely treifah life depends on it; our view Gemara holds hole disqualifies everywhere — no difficulty to cite liver — knew life depends here not there; or briefly Baal HaItur like latter version since stam "cut from spleen" in hilum and loose end; mishnah "cut from hilum" forbidden in eating also animal; "cut from loose end" forbidden in eating not animal — two explanations in one mishnah — forced; holds like latter version all permitted in cut; even we do not hold like Baal HaItur — in hilum animal forbidden — still difficult two explanations in one mishnah in one chapter — room to err cut in animal treifah; mishnah comes plainly cut organ from animal forbidden — teaches kosher; "even" may fit cut; also since cut causes pain at cut place as Rashi — punctured; half spleen thick half thin; if cuts middle between thick and thin — thick side also receives pain from both sides of cut — treifah because pains thick side too; teaches nevertheless kosher since cut body was on thin side — no affliction on thick side at all; examine. What Pri Chadash challenged Baal HaEphraim from lung punctured or deficient — what difficulty, difference between punctured and cut; complaint not on Baal HaEphraim but Gemara all Amoraim who challenged — should be comfortable one version for two versions in Gemara; no difficulty — lung removed treifah obvious no distinction punctured and cut; but spleen removed kosher — cut is removed not like hole that pains more — and to me.`,
    '2#ד': `If flesh around whole. Taz, Shach, Pri Chadash agreed water clear and all the more murky is like hole — so Rav Rama in Darkei Moshe, not Bach who exaggerated measure to be lenient. Hard to understand "flesh whole" intent dinar-thickness — what teaches, all this testimony they saw before Rabbeinu Ephraim he permitted remaining beautiful and whole gold dinar — obvious; they explained we do not say since water there enough to finish all; even if dinar remained nevertheless treifah — forced from Torah say so in lung with tubes poured like pitcher — nevertheless we do not fear one tube or membrane will rot — why say so in spleen? What differs from all organs; also whole on every side I did not understand; why not mention flesh whole like dinar-thickness — main of permit. Therefore clear intent Taz end siman agreed Pri Chadash: if on every side not recognizable in spleen only inside middle afflicted with clear water, murky, putrefied, etc. — every side no dinar-thickness remainder nevertheless kosher. True Taz proof from internal lung deficiency no proof — lung main disqualification in membrane and tubes, flesh of lung irrelevant — internal deficiency kosher since membranes and tubes exist; spleen disqualification not in spleen membrane but body of spleen lest hole — if so inside also invalid; however in etrog we also say depends on internal deficiency and there too treifot not in membrane but need proof in body — we learned punctured spleen — what hole, whole and closed every side how hole applies except do not say hole since afflicted inside end will dominate outside and hole revealed — therefore properly brings proof from lung — if that concern also there membrane would dominate and puncture; we do not fear — no hole at all; this was incident before Rabbeinu Ephraim — swollen but flesh beautiful no flaw only swollen; commanded cut, water flowed, scraped every side found whole around only middle swollen — permitted; did not investigate dinar-thickness since only inside and every side whole — simple and clear; "until hilum" means swelling began in loose-end area visibly outside; when cut cavity spread onward like bubbles hard at head spreading until reached inside hilum; examined every side whole permitted; in Agudah said incident swelling in hilum not loose end — see; error in other books said loose end; these clear — no doubting Taz law — so Rabbeinu Ephraim's words.`,
    '3#_': `All attached to kereis called thick and no more — in Lechem Mishneh wrote after attachment to kereis also thick and rests on kereis but not attached; Gaon author of Kli Yakar and sages of Prague agreed; he too in number to forbid; afterward retracted — most authors unlike him, Ran and ShDa wrote what attached to kereis called thick and no more; truly per what I wrote and found in Perishah — reason treifah not from spleen but affliction called to kereis — clear all depends on attachment to kereis; nevertheless I incline lenient since issued from mouths of gedolei hador to be stringent; Lechem Mishneh also said for halacha not practice; conversely since after attachment place also thick — if primary what attached to kereis how Gemara stam in hilum — there is hilum nevertheless kosher; how stam in hilum Rashi in its thickness above — therefore if spleen came not punctured through and through only remainder and remainder below in extreme thinness until no doubt no dinar-thickness remainder — I declare treifah — called thick; but if remainder only we are not expert dinar measure need specifically until half — in this plain affliction more than half; if on thick side not attached I permit — two doubts: perhaps dinar-thickness, perhaps not; if you say no doubt which is thick place perhaps loose end and hole does not disqualify at all — likewise reverse — must permit.`,
    '4#_': `Thickness of gold dinar, etc. — I said to find measure partially — known in Torah Tabernacle vessels Ark Table golden altar overlay gold; presumably equal overlay measure given Moses from Sinai how thick little or much we may not change; these are change would be explained — see Tosafot end Chagigah and Menachot 96b who hold Table overlay like Ark overlay and two Tables like three Arks — see; we do not find three Tables only three Arks Moses made; they hold overlays parallel no difference Table and Ark; so in Midrash Tetzaveh gives measure copper altar overlay copper thick as gold altar overlay — all one, all overlays written stam equal without doubt; Bava Batra 12 explained for R' Yehudah Ark wall thickness finger of four fingers in handbreadth — see Rashi and Tosafot s.v. finger; three Arks one inside another — golden Ark outside overlaying wooden Ark third finger; end Chagigah we say thickness of gold dinar — behold dinar thickness third finger; so Midrash copper overlay to copper altar is gold dinar thickness — all overlays equal. For Tanna who holds wall thickness two fingers — do not force reality dinar gold — holds wooden Ark main was thickest; see Tosafot Chagigah s.v. for Moses overlay thin very light — and behold measure in any event no more than third finger. I in my weakness body and deficient mind darkened intellect cannot delve much to establish on hanging; whoever God graced broad mind expert in Torah hear and Joseph take to clarify as word and wage much from heaven receive to clarify doubt in Torah and mention forgotten. When I speak thus I raise superior words on small margarine doubt supplier lest forget end Chagigah sinners of Israel no Gehennom light — a fortiori from golden altar only dinar-thickness overlay fire does not consume it — all the more transgressors full of commandments like pomegranate. Tosafot in Midrash Moses wondered on this — impossible wood not burn; God said thus way of supernal fire consumes fire and does not destroy — wondered what Tosafot wanted — apparent contradiction: fire not consuming overlay not from love of holiness and commandment but nature of supernal fire — even bush not consumed; what relevance commandment protects from fire altar. However words simple — known on golden altar no supernal fire at all — priest morning evening brought coal pan burned incense; how "way of supernal fire" — what wanted fire there; truth Midrash place is Tanchuma as said only on copper altar copper overlay copper dinar-thickness fire always day and night Moses wondered wood not burn; God said thus way in supernal fire fire eats fire; and so copper altar elevation altar supernal fire was; those are Tosafot words — difficult why derive a fortiori from golden altar no coals only one pan morning evening not a fortiori from copper altar also only overlay dinar copper fire constant day night as written fire continually on altar — copper altar always 480 years until Solomon's Temple — therefore Tosafot wrote from copper altar cannot bring proof — Midrash Moses wondered God answered thus way fire etc. — no proof no a fortiori; therefore derive a fortiori from golden altar also dinar-thickness no supernal fire at all — no challenge — and to me; examine.`,
    '5#_': `And some stringent — see Taz responsa 98 wrote if two spleens and we know which correct which excess and punctured in hilum — kosher; challenge: if so what does Gemara challenge Rava who said punctured treifah from mishnah cut from spleen and kidneys forbidden eating — animal permitted — what difficulty — perhaps mishnah deals when cut from excess and teaches nevertheless mother's slaughter permits as above; truly animal itself permitted since cut excess as Taz; can answer. Know what Rivan and Rosh wrote regarding Bedi in ox — measures Sages gave all in large ox and ram and by their value we learn to estimate other animals; so Rosh explicitly in all measures as above regarding liver so dinar thickness; Rashba learned in large ox dinar measure less than half spleen thickness — in other animals also less; if half spleen thickness in small animal less than spleen thickness in ox — dinar thickness in other animals also less — all by value — and to me. What Bach challenged if half spleen thickness in small animal like dinar thickness — take that thickness estimate in large ox; Pri Chadash seif 1 agreed for law; Heaven forbid lenient — only to me Shach measure dinar in large ox henceforth all by value — if other animal no dinar needed even half spleen thickness not so large; Bach and Pri Chadash challenge Rashba and Rambam who hold all measures taught in large and small animals — dinar thickness in all animals ox and calf; difficulty in their place if so perforce half calf spleen thickness like dinar suffices for ox; must say Rambam and Rashba only to be stringent — perhaps measures Bedi or two olives in liver Sages said even in small; but to be lenient half spleen thickness in calf like dinar measure we do not say — concern to be stringent Sages gave measure only in large ox as Rivan; truly half calf spleen thickness not like dinar only by value — examine.`,
    '6#_': `Therefore hole does not disqualify — Rambam's words; Rashba wrote though doubt elder already taught leniency; Ran and acharonim for fear of elder's face did not return and doubted — Gemara compares fowl to animal — if no hilum conversely no loose end all treifah; per what I wrote reason hole in hilum treifah causes rot to kereis — if so Rambam right fowl not attached to kereis no connection plainly all like loose end considered. I brought slight proof for Rambam: teaches punctured crop punctured small intestines among those treifot in fowl — why not teach removed crop removed small intestines treifah — certainly treifah like Tosafot challenge in animal stomach; must be Tosafot and authors' version since hole disqualifies all the more removed; difficult from spleen removed kosher punctured treifah — need not version only treifah in hilum — in fowl exists in every manner treifah no difference at all; must say in fowl kosher every manner therefore Turei Chayim stringent for himself — Heaven forbid stringent against Rambam. Ask your elder and they will tell you: what we clarified above treifot of spleen puncture reach affliction to kereis — do not challenge beginning chapter these treifot enumerated 18 treifot including punctured spleen — included in hole in kereis as Tosafot wrote therefore did not enumerate deficiency in skull since treifah reason membrane; Tanna taught you 18 — perhaps proof for above Tosafot wrote therefore did not enumerate deficient lung and spinal deficiency one in something other in hanging cords etc. — difficult how included punctured spleen with other holes not considered alone all holes must be perforation through and through and punctured spleen also no dinar-thickness remained treifah — requires further study — R' Avira does not hold distinguish dinar gold thickness since holds any hole in spleen disqualifies — reason not affliction of kereis and dinar measure none — only hole we require in all holes and properly count as one; conclusion we hold dinar gold thickness and in hilum specifically — say treifot because of kereis; truly nevertheless do not count it — and examine: truly difficult for our view R' Akiva punctured treifah — explanation perforation through and through or without dinar-thickness remainder — nevertheless if peel and divide spleen that has dinar-thicknesses in its thickness into two until each not thick only dinar and cut one — not kosher for no hole — what does Gemara challenge from mishnah cut from spleen — perhaps cut thus and spleen forbidden animal permitted; must say since cut pains more our view even cut this way nevertheless like hole until no dinar remainder helps because pains more — therefore Gemara answers punctured alone cut alone as Rashi himself challenged every cut is hole — must say mishnah deals cut in thickness and we answer not like punctured — this descends and punctures until no dinar remainder gold and this has remainder; but cut entirely plainly worse than punctured every cut has hole in it; Tur wrote well "even" — examine.`,
  },
  'pitchei-teshuva': {
    '1#_': `In the thick head. Be'er Heitev seif 1 in name of Taz: even in thin place at beginning of thick head — treifah. So responsa Mahari of Beit HaLevi kelal 5 siman 55; so Pri Chadash; see responsa Avnei Nezer Orach Chaim part 2 siman 121 who ruled where around hole is skin recognizable as from its nature — so in thick place all acharonim agreed treifah, not like Taz seif 2; but where not actually in thick — kosher — see there. [See responsa Noda BiYehudah siman 16 explained plainly even in such case one must declare treifah — only investigated mixture there — see; even so all who are lenient relying on Avnei Nezer — we do not exalt them, for all Noda BiYehudah's words there revolve on what he decided at beginning of responsa there that one may not rely at all on Taz's permit of this hole entirely because disputants are many, acharonim and gedolei Yisrael; he himself in later responsa strongly upheld Taz's permit and below seif 2 I also brought many gedolei Yisrael agreeing with Taz to permit even actually in thick — plainly lenient in case not actually in thick did not lose.]`,
    '2#_': `Through and through. Be'er Heitev what he wrote regarding holes commonly found in calves' spleens; see responsa Me'il Tzedakah siman 17 his view to permit like Taz — see. [So ruled responsa Taz siman 71 — see; so ruled responsa Pnei Yehoshua siman 15; so responsa Shevut Yaakov part 2 siman 65 his view so and wrote even though stringent opinions exist, one who relies on lenient did not lose — see; see Shlah daf 74a s.v. spleen; responsa Noda BiYehudah Yoreh De'ah siman 17; responsa Pri Tevuah siman 2, 3, and 40; see responsa Tiferet Tzvi siman 6 ot 2; responsa Even Shoham siman 47, 48, 49 on this matter; see Sefer Tiferet Lemoshe whether hole found thus in lung — wrote from Nekudat HaKesef implies kosher like open palm; he disagrees and his view even created so with hole treifah unless most animals were so — then we would say rabbeitehu — see well; see responsa Noda BiYehudah second edition Yoreh De'ah siman 19.]`,
    '3#_': `Gold dinar. See Tiferet Lemoshe who proved this is in a large animal but in small according to value of its size — see.`,
    '4#_': `Kosher. Be'er Heitev; and what he wrote regarding spleen salted without nikkur — see responsa Hilchot Ketanot part 1 siman 291 who made supports to permit, not like Taz; but responsa Shevut Yaakov part 2 siman 69 his view to forbid and wrote so should be ruled except nevertheless if salted with meat and there is great loss perhaps lenient did not lose — see; see responsa Shemesh Tzedakah Yoreh De'ah part siman 34.`,
    '5#_': `With change of flesh. Be'er Heitev seif 4 in name of Shach that change of appearance, etc.; so Taz and Pri Chadash change of appearance alone kosher. However Turei Shabbos seif 4 elaborated to be stringent that wherever this change of appearance is found it is affliction; for us who cannot be expert we fear perhaps like flesh doctor scrapes — see; see responsa Noda BiYehudah Yoreh De'ah part siman 13 who disagrees and raised like above poskim change of appearance alone is no flaw at all — stringent should be stringent for himself and examine; but for others especially in loss worth relying on lenient. However wherever change of appearance found must check and see if no affliction in flesh; if found on flesh boil and it has change of appearance especially black appearance — affliction and treifah — only must cut if appearance dominates through and through; see there siman 14 wrote all this in boils; but if only slightly raised if flesh not strange to touch soft or somewhat mushy — not affliction and no stringency at all — see; see Peri Megadim.`,
    '6#_': `And rotted. Be'er Heitev regarding internal affliction; Pri Chadash and Chochmat Adam held plainly to be lenient; see Turei Shabbos seif 6 his view treifah and so appears Peri Megadim; however in Mishbetzot Zahav he states neither prohibition nor permit — see; see Mateh Yehudah kelal 89 seif 4 was lenient in Mishbetzot Zahav and so Chochmat Adam kelal 18 din 4 — see; see Chiddushei Maharam Schiff Chullin 55b wrote to permit plainly in this and concluded as I think I heard in such case they are uncertain whether need like dinar-thickness on one side or suffice on two sides — in my view even combined not needed — see; see Sefer Nachalat Azriel Chullin 55 who wrote all this if also flesh around whole but spleen skin alone does not save and explained Taz's words Be'er Heitev brought seif 1 and wrote he did not understand Nekudat HaKesef's attack — see; examiner in Nekudat HaKesef will see from him too not hidden one may explain Taz's words so — only wrote what is his source — see.`,
  },
  'nekudot-hakesef': {
    '1#_': `(Siman 43 in Taz seif 2) "It appears simple," etc. Wonder — simple, for we require dinar-thickness remain; and if he means even if remained and no skin punctured, only skin whole every side treifah — whence? Also what he wrote as they said heart punctured treifah — I do not know the source; on the contrary it appears must be perforation through and through completely; also what he wrote further proof from Orach Chaim — no proof at all — see there; and this requires further study.`,
    '2#_': `(There) "And I answered to permit, needless to say," etc. In my humble opinion there is no proof here to permit — not like deficiency of lung from outside: there lung punctured treifah because wind exits from it and external deficiency does not harm at all — nevertheless lung rises in inflation; not so here; we do not say in treifot "similar to similar." And who tells us the spleen was created punctured — if because skin surrounds hole inside perhaps membrane grew afterward; behold in hole found in small intestine Rashba wrote responsa siman 483 and this is his language: you asked hole found in small intestine, etc.; it appears from context created so at formation of animal; some people say thus way of most animals, etc. — we do not listen, we did not see so in animals at all; I asked expert butchers and they told me from goring of another animal thus their way, and from those gorings many matters arise in kereis, stomach, small intestine — therefore forbidden; do not heed those who permit, their words have no substance, end of his words; behold there too appears created so at formation — yet we fear perhaps made from animal's goring and healed until they think created at formation; so here too though appears created so — we fear perhaps from goring — safek d'oraisa to be stringent. Also what he wrote further proven from Rambam — not proven at all: since he informs us removed like punctured — created deficient is like removed; specifically when all created deficient; but recognizable hole from beginning of creation is like punctured by hand; and specifically when known clearly made from beginning of creation — not so here. Incident came before me in this law — I debated with my court and found no proof to permit — we declared treifah.`,
    '3#_': `(Taz seif 8) "And even in great loss one may rule so." This is what Shach wrote seif 9.`,
  },
  'kaf-hachayim': {
    '1#_': `(1) [Seif 1] If the spleen was removed — kosher, whether through illness or by hand or created deficient. Orach Chaim kelal 52 ot 11. As Kenesset HaGedolah in Hagahot Tur end ot 1.`,
    '2#_': `(2) And this is illness that shrank it — spleen is not treifah when shrunk and there is no measure for its growth; but if removed through illness that it dissolved — treifah, for it began dissolving in hilum, namely rotted flesh doctor scrapes and treifah — how return to kosher by removal; therefore truly treifah; Shulchan Aruch relied on kidney (below siman 44 seif 6); Peleti siman 44 end ot 8; however Einayim LaMishpat siman 22 ot 2 and in his book She'erit Yosef siman 44 ot 5 disagrees and his view to permit even removed through dissolving illness — see there. But Mechaber in this siman ot 10 agreed to Peleti and disagreed with Rav Yekutiel siman 50 ot 2 who permitted; so Chochmat Adam kelal 18 ot 8 like Peleti; Zivchei Shelamim ot 1; Turei Zahav siman 59 ot 15; and see below seif 2 in hagahah.`,
    '3#_': `(3) [Seif 2] The spleen one end thick, etc.; and if punctured in thick place, etc. That removed kosher and punctured treifah — because punctured pains more and no longer lives; but cut does not pain so much and kosher — Beit Yosef, Levush, Zivchei Tzedek ot 2; Perishah ot 2 wrote affliction worse for hole causes kereis on it to rot unlike cut — see; Beit Dino as Kenesset HaGedolah in Hagahot Beit Yosef ot 11; Zivchei Tzedek there.`,
    '4#_': `(4) There: if punctured in thick head, etc.; even though on thick side somewhat thin in width — nevertheless forbidden there — Taz seif 1; so Shlah daf 75a; Kenesset HaGedolah Hagahot Tur ot 6; Pri Chadash ot 1; Eliyah Rabba in seif 3; Mishnat Zaken ot 1 wrote Taz's intent simple: in thick part on its sides and head thinness — all included in name "thick" and treifah wherever punctured there — Mechaber ot 2; Chochmat Adam kelal 18 end ot 1; Zivchei Tzedek end ot 2; Einayim LaMishpat siman 22 ot 4; Beit Yosef Avraham in Sha'ar HaTziyun ot 1; Kometz ot there; and on thin side kosher in entire that side — Shlah there; Kenesset HaGedolah there; Beit Yosef Avraham there.`,
    '5#_': `(5) The spleen has thin skin on its flesh and also membrane on thick side — not from its body but covering as Shulchan Aruch siman 64 seif 10; if spleen punctured even if that membrane whole and not punctured — treifah — Taz seif 2; Kenesset HaGedolah Hagahot Tur ot 5; Pri Chadash ot 1; Eliyah Rabba seif 2; Beit Yehudah ot 2; Sha'arei Zahav ot 1; Zivchei Rokeach ot 2 wrote Taz's intent simple: if no dinar-thickness remained only combined with membrane on spleen which is impure fat as explained siman 64 seif 10 — that does not complete; so Mechaber end ot 3 in name of several poskim; Einayim LaMishpat there ot 6; Turei Zahav siman 59 ot 5; Beit Yosef Avraham Sha'ar HaTziyun ot 4; Beit Yitzchak in Amud HaZahav ot 1; Kometz there in Asaron ot 15. But thin skin on its body joins for gold dinar for all — Einayim LaMishpat there.`,
    '6#_': `(6) If found in some district calves with perforation through and through in spleen at thick head and around hole from inside spleen skin surrounds recognizable created so; each time hole in one place; some say way of most calves — to permit — Taz seif 2; so responsa Taz siman 71 to permit; so Pri Tevuah ot 2 in name of several poskim; however Shach in Nekudat HaKesef attacked Taz's words; so Pri Chadash ot 2 attacked; so Rav Torat Yekutiel siman 50 ot 2; Sha'arei Efraim ot 3 wrote their attack only if found thus in one calf or minority of calves per Taz's reasoning even so only one kosher for reasons he wrote; but if we stood on investigation that in that district majority of calves so and we see most calves not slaughtered majority remain and grow as everywhere and multiply on land and clarified clearly so — then appears not hole but way of growth — no prohibition on majority slaughtered found so; nevertheless must be careful absolute clarity majority so exist and remainder standing to grow grow like all animals in other districts becoming large — death and multiplying not common among them; if impossible to stand on clarification — do not be lenient — see. So Mishnat Zaken end ot 2; Mechaber ot 4; Einayim LaMishpat there ot 10; Zivchei Shelamim ot 3; Turei Zahav there ot 7; Kometz ot 12; Zivchei Tzedek ot 5; however in great loss whatever has side and slight proof — rabbeitehu — even if opposite side — be lenient; on teacher to investigate clarify — and God was with the judge — Mechaber there; Einayim LaMishpat there; Zivchei Tzedek there.`,
  },
  'mateh-yehonatan': {
    '1#_': `(Siman 43 seif 2) And if punctured with hole not perforation through and through. Shach seif 1 — Rashi's language "and if there remained in thickness of its wall," etc. — see his words; Bach wants to prove from these Rashi words that kereis punctured and spleen seals it kosher — otherwise needle in body cavity; or we say from kereis came to spleen therefore not treifah because spleen seals its hole — perforce. However one may say Rashi goes his way in chapter 1 daf 45 s.v. tarfesha — heart fat implies he holds sealing of pure fat helps even not attached in creation; he explained there if tarfesha of heart stuck to lung it does not seal because like hat-shaped fat not attached in creation; nevertheless one may say Rashi holds even not in creation it seals if so — for us who hold if not attached in creation does not seal — spleen too does not seal.`,
    '2#_': `(There Taz seif 2) I was asked in a district where calves found with perforation through and through, etc. What he wrote to permit because common in a district — one may say rabbeitehu; we wrote several times in name of Rashba's responsa we are not expert in rabbeitehu except if in entire that species this flaw exists — not if found in some without this flaw we do not say rabbeitehu. What he wants to permit because round hole created so is category deficiency kosher in spleen — prohibition only if punctured afterward — from Ramban's words appears opposite: Ramban wrote two spleens attached on thick side treifah; so Rama below hagahah seif 5 — because he holds all excess considered removed — that excess and its place with it and as if spleen punctured in hilum as Beit Yosef siman 41. If so in spleen since created so not like punctured spleen but created deficient and kosher — why did Ramban write if found like spleen on thick side treifah — even if we say like actual removal nevertheless only deficiency that does not treifah spleen at all — must say not like Taz who calls it hole if created so treifah; so when incident came before Avnei Nezer he did not fill his heart to be lenient in this case at all.`,
    '3#_': `(In hagahah) And even if cut in thin place kosher. Language "even" not precise — see Shach seif 20; Avnei Nezer — poskim divided whether cut in thick place treifah or not; their dispute in that Rav Avira said only removed but punctured treifah; challenges from cutting from fetus permitted from spleen and kidneys forbidden; answers punctured alone cut alone; afterward halacha not like Rav Avira — only in loose ends not in hilum; commentators now that we distinguish hilum and loose end we do not distinguish punctured and cut; one may say also cut treifah; mishnah "cut from spleen" forbidden but animal itself permitted deals with cut in loose end; therefore Tur and Rama also hold now per conclusion we do not distinguish puncture and cut — also cut treifah like punctured — only if cut in thick place affliction in thick place treifah; but if cut on thin side meaning entire thick place cut only cut was in thin place and thick removed too — certainly kosher since affliction on thin side kosher; therefore "even" refers to cut — even though cut we could say treifah since if cut in thick treifah — here thick also removed by cut — teaches nevertheless kosher since cut on thin side — no affliction on thick side; see Pri Chadash who asks per what Gemara answers punctured alone cut alone — what challenge above 47b lung punctured or deficient — what deficient, if external same as punctured except internal; teaches internal deficiency called deficiency — perhaps internal deficiency not called deficiency; mishnah deficient means cut — no need punctured alone cut alone — and to me: punctured alone etc. regarding spleen deficient kosher unlike if deficient treifah — certainly no distinction punctured and cut; rule wherever punctured treifah also created deficient treifah automatically also cut treifah — only spleen where punctured treifah nevertheless specifically in hilum but in loose end kosher — therefore this rule not in spleen; properly distinction punctured and cut unlike lung — challenges well.`,
    '4#_': `(In hagahah) And if water in spleen. See Taz seif 8 and 9; what Rama meant to compare this law to internal deficiency of lung — apparently not similar at all: there regarding lung flesh deficiency does not reduce anything for all lung treifot depend on membrane — membrane whole flesh neither helps nor harms; not so spleen where treifah depends on flesh — one may say internal deficiency is called deficiency; must be Taz's explanation this certainly no treifah in spleen except if punctured; since spleen whole every side without external deficiency — no hole on it — only one may say nevertheless treifah lest in end will puncture outward — therefore lung poured like pitcher kosher and we do not fear membrane will puncture — so here even if punctured inside and dissolved we do not fear perhaps all dissolved; see responsa Taz wrote if two spleens and one punctured perforation through and through kosher since both like removed — again no treifah applies; from this proven not his view from challenge on Rav Avira who said spleen punctured treifah from mishnah cut from spleen forbidden eating but itself kosher; per Taz words can establish mishnah deals found after slaughter two spleens — then hole does not disqualify and therefore itself kosher — must say even with two spleens hole disqualifies for though like removed nevertheless not removed — treifah from affliction of hole and treifah.`,
  },
  'yad-avraham': {
    '1#_': `(Siman 43 seif 2) The spleen, etc. — perforation through and through treifah. See Taz: I was asked calves found, etc., I answered to permit, etc.; so Mateh Yehudah kelal 89 wrote to permit hole created in organs without cavity; so Taz siman 71; Noda BiYehudah siman 17 lenient on hole created in spleen because novelty as Beit Yosef — you have in it only its novelty — punctured by thorn or illness; nevertheless in great loss rely on Taz in his case; but large ox implies in Kerem Shlomo do not be lenient. Mateh Yehudah also wrote to permit in great loss internal deficiency in spleen as Taz this siman and Kerem Shlomo.`,
    '2#_': `(Shulchan Aruch seif 5) Two spleens found. Sefer Taz siman 98 permitted with two spleens one small punctured in hilum like Barda siman 35; so Shulchan Aruch siman 35 and 44; difficult from Chullin 55 Rav Avira from Rava: only removed spleen kosher but punctured treifah; Rabbi Yosi bar Avin challenges cutting from fetus permitted from spleen and kidneys forbidden eating — animal itself permitted; what does he challenge Rav Avira — perhaps mishnah deals with two spleens and permit recognizable e.g. smaller than other and cut from permitted spleen; per Taz no treifah disqualifies permitted organ; one may say therefore mishnah does not deal cutting from excess spleen — if so why teach cutting forbidden in eating — reason because said in animal "that you shall eat" expounded whole not deficient — see Rashi; meaning only when cutting from required organ must be whole animal and he lacks by cutting; but cutting from excess organ not relevant to forbid — not whole applies; so Tosafot there 67 regarding horns in animal not forbidden because "that" whole not deficient — nothing deficient; if so necessarily only one spleen deals.`,
    '3#_': `(There seif 6) Spleen of fowl, etc. Therefore hole does not disqualify. See Taz challenged Rambam who explained what Levi taught all treifot Sages enumerated in animal corresponding in fowl — refers to mishnah treifot not Amora treifot; treifot of kidney and spleen they did not enumerate in animal in mishnah. Taz challenged we find this language Gemara 54 Rav Pappa's house struck kidney killed — came before Rabbi Abba — you have only what Sages enumerated — that certainly not mishnah alone but all Amoraim enumerated; if so whence to distinguish and explain other matter. It appears to me Rambam's explanation necessary from sugya Piskei Avodah Zarah 57 Rav Shemuel thigh dislocated in fowl kosher; Tosafot forced there implies specifically fowl permits not animal — challenges beraisa Levi all treifot; per our master it is spacious Levi refers only mishnah treifot and dislocated thigh not in mishnah; afterward I saw Rashba responsa 294 and Turei Chayim so himself; further appears this Levi beraisa arranged from Tannaim before (see Rashi beginning Beitzah); therefore "Sages enumerated" in mishnah and beraisa specifically; not like Rabbi Abba "Sages enumerated" who was Amora unlike Sages in beraisa — only Tannaim mentioned in mishnah and beraisa; further Niddah 18 even Amora language calls Sages only mishnah and beraisa not Amora sugya; so Be'er Sheva and Turei Chayim chapter 35. With this also Pri Chadash's difficulty on Rambam from Piskei Avodah Zarah 56 comparing fowl lung to animal for treifot though not similar for cutting testicles — we would also compare spleen of fowl to animal for treifot stringently; per what I said to me Levi treifot of spleen not mentioned in mishnah and beraisa unlike lung treifot mentioned in mishnah.`,
  },
  'yad-ephraim': {
    '1#_': `In thick head perforation through and through. See Be'er Heitev; see Noda BiYehudah siman 16 treifot fell in slaughterhouse via one spleen punctured in hilum i.e. thin place on thick side where thick side also thins and hole folded skin every side inside as if from nature; this spleen taken from mixture of 40–50 spleens from animals slaughtered those days; those already separated from slaughterhouse and left kitchen — everything that separated applies; only like 8–10 animals remaining in slaughterhouse back parts and also part of face side taken last — rov ba'alei batim does not apply. If we knew the animal from which spleen — do not rely on Taz and Taz for many disagree and we would declare treifah definitively; we were in ox where even lenient only mentioned calves — perhaps they agree in ox not rabbeitehu (perhaps in ox typo and should read a fortiori in ox); but because of mixture one may say back part forbidden without nikkur and nikkur great effort like lamb in its skin not called worth honoring — Ran wrote must be Rabbi Yehudah for every person; for Israel forbidden not Rabbi Yehudah. Also combine Taz's reasoning permit applies even in ox; Nekudat HaKesef forbade only from doubt — rely on poskim large cut or live animal not worth honoring; also Gaon Rav Ezriel in Beit David siman 110 explained part permitted whole permitted; here face parts permitted back parts permitted since great loss Yom Kippur eve urgency — permit only must sell one to gentile dry-for-dry; also combine lenient opinion Pri Chadash even on thick side nevertheless on thin side of that side kosher though rejected opinion — combination here; face parts taken yesterday last rov ba'alei batim does not apply — declare treifah — see; see Peri Megadim part 2 siman 101 hole in hilum inside skin surrounds hole each time in thin side of hilum recognizable skin from nature — rely to permit since many permit even thick place; in our case many times when occurred found only thin place around — learn rabbeitehu; so I ruled practically — see; Noda BiYehudah siman 17 punctured spleen in calves like Taz's incident common district practiced lenient formerly — great loss common much — teacher should not change and permit per their custom — see; Peri Megadim there and Noda BiYehudah wrote combine reasoning thin side in thick place not law of thick place even branch; Peri Megadim so from Rashi; Mechaber rejected not worth relying even branch ab initio Heaven forbid attribute to Rashi; Noda BiYehudah siman 16 many branches — combination not comfortable — see; Mechaber punctured spleen in calves if apparent majority of calves so eye sees grow multiply proven rabbeitehu — permit for many permit; great loss whatever side slight proof rabbeitehu even opposite side lenient; Kerem Shlomo if spleen removed through dissolving completely treifah — see his words siman 44; Torat Yekutiel wrote to permit; Mechaber agreed to Peleti — see; Tiferet Lemoshe wrote if created so not thick in hilum like dinar kosher — no worse than created deficient without spleen at all; therefore they said in kidney shrunk in creation kosher — see; Mechaber wrote his words appear correct; see Turei Zahav 141:45 in name of Teshuvat Hashlishi and Pri Chadash lenient in great loss; Mechaber brought from Menachot permit without doubt even though Lechem Mishneh wrote only for halacha — therefore permitted in great loss at least not like Peleti who sided stringent; see Mechaber in name of Chagurat Shmuel if where not attached hole found skin around recognizable created so — permit even not great loss — agreed — see. If this hole in thick place not attached place has slight measure doubt if like gold dinar thickness and no great loss — be stringent; if cut there Pri Tevuah's view to permit — dispute of rabbis and two doubts not like Pri Megadim doubt deficiency knowledge what is hilum — see; Peleti proved from Bava Batra and end Chagigah dinar thickness third finger; Mechaber wrote this no proof — see; Mechaber less than half kosher teacher should ensure less slightly minimal; every spleen require remain less than half whether ox or calf as Teshuvat Hashlishi and Peleti not like Pri Chadash in Kuntres Aleph; if punctured in thin place on thick and half or slightly less of that thin place remained kosher — see Mishbetzot Zahav so Mechaber; if punctured two sides opposite each other and between remained like dinar-thickness from spleen flesh kosher as Teshuvat Hashlishi — must estimate well flesh between is slightly less than half spleen; so holes not opposite — see Teshuvat Hashlishi. Mechaber if occurred not opposite in large ox estimate less than half thickness — need not measure between holes — suffices slight measure whenever appears flesh between two holes healthy kosher; if boil in hilum place attached to kereis no flesh only boil skin — if dinar-thickness under boil from other side even not from kereis side kosher — so Mechaber in name of Dvar Moshe; see Sefer Beit Yehudah 114 spleen with large boil full dust fine sand exposed above no dinar-thickness below — Rav Mohar"i Tzror ruled since tins not mentioned stam as its explanation kosher — brought Mechaber; to me requires further study: deficiency of flesh disqualifies — perhaps tins invalid never return to be flesh; also perhaps sand fine worse than tins — tins from water this complete dissolution — requires further study; see Shevut Yaakov part 2 siman 65 round hole found in calves' spleen; in Lechem Mishneh brought stringent opinions — relying on lenient did not lose as proofs in name of Mateh Yehudah; also since found only in calves when grown holes sealed like all spleens — so created; Shach doubted Rama's leniency in kids and lambs — nevertheless appears no stringency — see Even Shoham siman 47 on holes found in spleen.`,
    '2#_': `If there remained beneath it like thickness. Be'er Heitev; Shevut Yaakov part 3 siman 43 spleen swollen in middle outside both sides no flaw — permit; all the more if combining both sides like two gold dinars kosher; wrote responsa Pri Tevuah siman 2 law perforation through and through in spleen on thick side.`,
    '3#_': `Therefore no hole. Be'er Heitev; see Mechaber brought many rishonim and acharonim — we hold punctured spleen of fowl permitted; Bach wrote listener to Ra'ah who is stringent should say to him holy; Mechaber wrote intent he sanctifies himself in what is permitted to him. If two spleens found in fowl — permit even Maharshal — not like Lechem Mishneh.`,
  },
};
